  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Venu Madhav vs Food Inspector on 4 February, 2019 Author: R.K.Gauba Bench: R.K.Gauba $~28 * In The High Court Of Delhi At New Delhi + Crl.M.C. 596/2019 & Crl.M.A. 2484/2019 Venu Madhav ..... Petitioner Through: Mr. Bipin Kalappa, Adv. versus Food Inspector ..... Respondent Through: Mr. Sanjeev Sabharwal, App for the State . Coram: Hon'Ble Mr. Justice R.K.Gauba Order",
    "facts": "On the criminal complaint (CC no. 43452/2016) instituted by the respondent alleging offence punishable under Prevention of Food Adulteration Act, 1954, a number of persons were summoned as accused they including the petitioner herein shown in the array as eighth accused (A- 8). The said order dated 04.12.2017 is stated to be under challenge in the court of Sessions by Crl. Rev.No. 39/2018 preferred by the respondent. It appears from the documents on record, as indeed the submissions of the counsel for the petitioner that notice of the above said petition was duly served on the latter (the petitioner) and he along with certain others had appeared before the revisional court through counsel. The presence of the CRL.M.C. 596/2019 page 1 of 3 petitioner is indicated in the proceedings recorded by the revisional court on 12.12.2018.",
    "arguments": "The counsel for the petitioner submits that he had been engaged and duly instructed by the petitioner to appear before the revisional court, he having already filed his reply to the revision petition. The counsel for the petitioner submits no such specific order requiring personal appearance Venu Madhav vs Food Inspector on 4 February, 2019 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/151218616/ 1 of the petitioner has been passed by the revisional court.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "The counsel for the petitioner submits that he had been engaged and duly instructed by the petitioner to appear before the revisional court, he having already filed his reply to the revision petition. The counsel for the petitioner submits no such specific order requiring personal appearance Venu Madhav vs Food Inspector on 4 February, 2019 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/151218616/ 1 of the petitioner has been passed by the revisional court.",
